---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: "Our Feedback | The Café"
description: "What customers tell The Café in Leavenworth, KS: every survey card and web survey summed up, good and bad, what people asked for, and what we changed."
ogDescription: "Every survey The Café in Leavenworth has had, summed up: the ratings, what customers asked for, and what we changed."
pageCss: "/assets/css/feedback.css"
---
{#- ===========================================================
    /feedback — every customer survey, summed up, good and bad
    (client 2026-10-27; CONTACT-PLAN.md in CafeWork, RV-2).

    Nothing here is typed by hand except feedback.json:
      the totals, months, quotes   src/_data/feedbackStats.json, made by
                                   the kitchen PC (Manage -> Survey -> For
                                   the website) and replaced whole
      what people asked for,       src/_data/feedback.json, written by hand
      "You said, we did"           from the comments, as counted themes
    feedback.11tydata.js builds this page only once there is a survey, and
    the footer links it only then.

    The rules: every answer is in the totals, the Okay and Poor ones too
    (a page of only the good ones is what the FTC's 2024 reviews rule bars,
    and people trust it less). A customer's words only with the survey's
    share box ticked, with a first name and initial at most. No staff names.
    No star-rating markup: Google doesn't show stars for reviews a business
    publishes about itself, and the markup for them risks a penalty.
    =========================================================== -#}
{%- set s = feedbackStats %}
{%- macro pct(n, of) %}{{ ((n / of) * 100) | round | int if of else 0 }}%{% endmacro %}
{%- macro monthName(m) %}{{ ["January","February","March","April","May","June","July","August","September","October","November","December"][(m.slice(5, 7) | int) - 1] }} {{ m.slice(0, 4) }}{% endmacro %}

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="feedback-heading">
    <div class="container feedback">
        <h1 id="feedback-heading">Our feedback</h1>
        <p class="feedback-lede">
            Every survey our customers have filled in since {{ s.since | dayDate("monthDay") if s.since else "we started asking" }},
            on paper at the counter or on our website: <strong>{{ s.total }} so far</strong>, good and bad, all counted here.
            We read every one.
        </p>

        <h2 class="feedback-h">How we're doing</h2>
        <ul class="ratings" role="list">
            {%- for q in s.ratings %}
            {%- set great = q.counts[0][1] %}{% set good = q.counts[1][1] %}
            <li class="rating">
                <p class="rating-head">
                    <span class="rating-name">{{ q.label }}</span>
                    <span class="rating-sum">{{ pct(great + good, q.answered) }} Great or Good</span>
                </p>
                <div class="bar" aria-hidden="true">
                    {%- for pair in q.counts %}{% if pair[1] %}<span class="bar-{{ pair[0] | lower }}" style="flex-grow: {{ pair[1] }};"></span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
                </div>
                <p class="rating-counts">
                    {%- for pair in q.counts %}<span class="key key-{{ pair[0] | lower }}">{{ pair[0] }} {{ pair[1] }}</span>{% endfor %}
                    <span class="rating-of">of {{ q.answered }} who answered</span>
                </p>
            </li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ul>

        {%- if s.months.length > 1 %}
        <h2 class="feedback-h">Month by month</h2>
        <p class="feedback-note">The share who rated each one Great.</p>
        <div class="months-wrap">
            <table class="months">
                <thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Surveys</th>{% for q in s.ratings %}{% set known = survey.ratings | where("name", q.name) %}<th scope="col">{{ known[0].short if known.length else q.label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    {%- for m in s.months | reverse %}
                    <tr><th scope="row">{{ monthName(m.month) }}</th><td>{{ m.total }}</td>{% for q in m.ratings %}<td>{{ pct(q.counts[0][1], q.answered) if q.answered else "–" }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
                    {%- endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- if feedback.changes.length %}
        <h2 class="feedback-h">You said, we did</h2>
        <ul class="changes" role="list">
            {%- for c in feedback.changes %}
            <li><p class="said">{{ c.said }}</p><p class="did">{{ c.did }}</p></li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- if feedback.asked.length %}
        <h2 class="feedback-h">What you've asked for</h2>
        <ul class="asked" role="list">
            {%- for a in feedback.asked %}
            <li><span>{{ a.label }}</span><span class="asked-n">{{ a.count }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- if s.quotes.length %}
        <h2 class="feedback-h">In your words</h2>
        <p class="feedback-note">From customers who said we could share them.</p>
        <ul class="quotes" role="list">
            {%- for q in s.quotes %}
            <li>
                <blockquote><p>{{ q.text }}</p></blockquote>
                <p class="quote-who">{{ q.name or "A customer" }}, {{ q.date | dayDate("monthDay") }}</p>
            </li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}

        <div class="feedback-cta">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/survey">Tell us how we did</a>
            {%- if site.reviews.googleUrl %}
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="{{ site.reviews.googleUrl }}" rel="noopener">Leave a Google review</a>
            {%- endif %}
        </div>
        <p class="feedback-note">Last updated {{ s.updated | dayDate("monthDay") }}.</p>
    </div>
</section>
